  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The function decides the class: farming makes it rural, whatever its size.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Water came first because every other activity depends on it.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Scattered farmsteads are dispersed; clusters round a point are nucleated.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The houses follow the route, which gives the linear pattern its name.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Site is local ground; situation is regional position.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Rent peaks where access peaks, and access peaks at the centre.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The Burgess model rings the centre: CBD, transition, housing, suburbs, commuter belt.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The level is the share at one date; the rate is its change over time.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Several towns merging along their edges form a conurbation.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Threshold is the minimum demand; range is the maximum distance customers will travel.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    A university has a high threshold and a long range, so it sits at the top of the hierarchy.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Migration adds people; the young urban population then adds more by natural increase.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Growth outruns housing, water, drains and transport.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The 1976 decision moved the capital to a central, less congested site.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Deliberate layout is the mark of a planned settlement.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The hilltop camp and the cocoa hinterland made it the largest indigenous city in Africa.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Function is what the place does; form is the pattern it makes.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Its limit is the distance a worker will travel each day.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Farming supports more people where the land and the rain allow it.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Cheap land next to the centre attracts storage and trade, and old housing decays.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    A route or a raised bank is the only buildable line in many landscapes.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    It sits at the bottom of the hierarchy, with perhaps a kiosk and a well.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Size and services rise together up the ladder.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    The young and able leave, leaving the old and the children.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "D", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
    Narrow lanes, no drains and no piped water make them vulnerable.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 22.0pt)[
